# {{PROJECT_NAME}} Coding Standards

This document governs newly written and materially changed code. Apply the
selected industry language baseline first while treating verified formatter,
compiler, CI, public-contract, compatibility, security, privacy, and platform
requirements as hard constraints. Existing project conventions are required
compatibility evidence, not an automatic reason to preserve weaker legacy style.

## Authority and conflict order

1. Safety, privacy, legal, public-contract, compatibility, compiler, build, and
   CI constraints that the project must satisfy.
2. The selected industry baseline for the language of each changed file.
3. Existing project rules and local conventions that do not conflict with the
   first two levels.
4. Explicitly approved team or personal preferences for otherwise undecided cases.

For a style-only conflict, prefer the industry baseline inside the approved
change. For a mechanically enforced conflict, keep the build green, record the
difference below, and propose configuration migration separately. Never hide a
conflict or expand a focused task into repository-wide reformatting.

